Dear Elizabeth,

Nice to hear from you.
I am very sorry I haven=E2=80=99t replied to you sooner; your previous emai=
l must have slipped through my inbox.
Reading your notes now, I got the feeling that some of the behavior you obs=
erve may be due to the =E2=80=9Csub homogeneity=E2=80=9D of the gradient of=
 the softplus activation. We used that concept here<https://urldefense.com/=
v3/__https://arxiv.org/pdf/2403.00720__;!!Mak6IKo!OydniWBdL1EMFFkcgafD6uIy8=
gCiRLsQFMm6VxhY8rkBFRAz8PfhsxbUF1zyB6F_qZaOlcpkD1C1JoaTAL8N4A$ > to show th=
at certain architectures have unique fixed points. This may be extended to =
discuss fixed points of the gradient flow map.

Together with the Swiss Roll observations (geometric contraction, alternati=
ng cone behavior under different losses), I feel there is a coherent story =
forming, but I would really value your judgment on which aspects are most w=
orth pursuing. I can share any plots and codes I have and organize an updat=
ed note if you're interested.

Yes, please, if you can share an updated note, that would help me get a bet=
ter feeling of your observations and where you are aiming to.

I should be honest about why I didn't send a second note sooner. Part of it=
 was the semester getting busy, but a bigger part was that I struggled to u=
nderstand what I was seeing. I could describe the phenomena but didn't feel=
 I had the background to explain them properly. That, combined with the wor=
ry that the results might just be trivial, made me hesitant to share work I=
 couldn't fully account for. I also think my first note was overambitious i=
n its framing. I was excited and probably overclaimed relative to what I co=
uld actually justify. I'm trying to be more careful this time.

Don=E2=80=99t worry. I am the one who didn't answer and should be sorry.

On a more personal note, I am currently a sophomore at UW=E2=80=93Madison g=
raduating early (around Fall 2026) and I am currently exploring research di=
rections for this summer. The intersection of nonlinear Perron=E2=80=93Frob=
enius theory and learning dynamics is the direction I find most compelling.=
 If there is any possibility of a remote collaboration, or if you could poi=
nt me toward related groups or opportunities, I would be very grateful.

I have to admit I am very busy this summer, as I=E2=80=99ve already taken o=
n several supervision projects.
I will ask my former postdoc, Pietro Deidda, if he would be willing to help=
 supervise a summer project collaboration with you.
Alternatively, I know Renato Cavalcante is interested in topics at the inte=
rface of PF and ML, maybe you could contact him to see if he is interested/=
availability: https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://sites.google.com/site/ren=
atoresearch/__;!!Mak6IKo!OydniWBdL1EMFFkcgafD6uIy8gCiRLsQFMm6VxhY8rkBFRAz8P=
fhsxbUF1zyB6F_qZaOlcpkD1C1JoZo9sK3nQ$=20

Best wishes,

=E2=80=94Francesco

