Dear Dr. Tudisco,
I am an undergraduate student in mathematics and computer science at UW=E2=
=80=93Madison. I am writing because I recently observed a Perron=E2=80=93Fr=
obenius=E2=80=93type phenomenon in gradient-based learning dynamics, and I =
noticed potential connections with your work on nonlinear Perron=E2=80=93Fr=
obenius theory.
Very roughly, in a simple gradient-descent model with a nonnegative paramet=
rization (via an appropriate non-linear activation and loss), the iterates =
exhibit an exponential contraction in Hilbert=E2=80=99s projective metric.

I would be very grateful if you could tell me:


  1.
whether such a Hilbert=E2=80=93projective contraction phenomenon has appear=
ed in the literature for gradient-based dynamics, or if it is essentially n=
ew;

  2.
whether you are aware of any work connecting gradient flows or gradient des=
cent with nonlinear Perron=E2=80=93Frobenius theory or cone-contraction fra=
meworks;

  3.
and whether interpreting training dynamics through Hilbert=E2=80=99s projec=
tive geometry seems mathematically natural from your perspective.


If this is of interest, I would be very happy to send you a short note with=
 the precise setup and some experimental results.

Thank you very much for your time.

Best regards,

Xinyang Wen

